      {
        "id": 29542,
        "name": "msbq",
        "username": "msbq",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/msbq/{size}/2824_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-17T16:15:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Civi&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Civi\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The sets do follow comic genres, and so far we seem to have had:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Silver Age</li>\n<li>Dark/Street</li>\n<li>Mystical</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Off the top of my head this leaves the follow possible genres to follow up with:</p>\n<p>-Time Travel (Golden Age and Dark Future styles)<br>\n-Cosmic (aliens, and universe spanning troubles)<br>\n-Multiverse (Alternate Realities - It’s in the title and has never been touched on yet)<br>\n-Meta Event (The big finish, it should draw everything together and radicaly change the game)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This succession seems most plausible to me. I’ve read comics since I’ve been able to read and these all resonate pretty clearly.<br>\nThe closest thing we’ve got to a Time Traveler is Tachyon’s Barry-Allan-esque super speed.</p>",
